{%- comment -%}
  Bassface collection card — image, then a title row with a corner arrow.

  A snippet, not a section: it is the atom the search overlay and the All
  Collections page are both built from. Dawn's own card-collection.liquid is
  left in place for the stock sections that still render it.

  Accepts:
    collection - a collection object. Required. Renders a placeholder when
                 blank so the theme editor still composes with nothing chosen.
    ratio      - image aspect ratio, e.g. '7 / 6'. Optional; falls back to
                 11/12. Passed by the CONSUMER, not chosen per collection —
                 the boards use 21/23, 11/12 and 7/6 for the same card in three
                 different places, so the shape belongs to the composition.
    sizes      - the `sizes` attribute. Pass the real column width.
    loading    - 'lazy' (default) or 'eager'.
    title      - overrides the collection's own title. Optional; for the
                 automatic all-products collection, which Shopify titles
                 "Products" and nobody can rename.

  Usage:
    {%- render 'bf-collection-card', collection: collection, ratio: '7 / 6' -%}

  The image is collection.image when the merchant has set one, falling back to
  the first product's featured image — which is what Shopify shows in the admin
  and avoids an empty box on a collection nobody has given artwork to.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign loading = loading | default: 'lazy'
  assign sizes = sizes | default: '(min-width: 834px) 25vw, 50vw'

  assign card_image = collection.image
  if card_image == blank
    assign card_image = collection.products.first.featured_image
  endif
-%}

<a
  class="collection-card"
  href="{{ collection.url | default: '#' }}"
  {% if ratio != blank %}
    style="--collection-card-ratio: {{ ratio }};"
  {% endif %}
>
  <span class="collection-card__media">
    {%- if card_image -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Empty alt: the card is one link whose accessible name is the title
        below, so a described image would announce the collection twice.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <img
        class="collection-card__image"
        src="{{ card_image | image_url: width: 800 }}"
        srcset="
          {{ card_image | image_url: width: 400 }} 400w,
          {{ card_image | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w,
          {{ card_image | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w,
          {{ card_image | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w
        "
        sizes="{{ sizes }}"
        width="{{ card_image.width }}"
        height="{{ card_image.height }}"
        alt=""
        loading="{{ loading }}"
      >
    {%- else -%}
      {{ 'collection-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'collection-card__image' }}
    {%- endif -%}
  </span>

  <span class="collection-card__row">
    {%- comment -%}
      `title` overrides collection.title. The one caller today is the All
      Collections page's first card: Shopify's automatic all-products
      collection is titled "Products", which reads as a category next to
      "Afrojack" and "Alesso", and the board labels it "All Products". The
      merchant cannot rename an automatic collection, so the label has to come
      from the caller.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <span class="collection-card__title">
      {{- title | default: collection.title | default: 'Collection' -}}
    </span>
    <span class="collection-card__arrow">
      {%- render 'bf-icon', icon: 'arrow-up-right', size: 22 -%}
    </span>
  </span>
</a>
